<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33689" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">panthērīnus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		1. panthera, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of a panther</i> or <i>panthers.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pellis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 11, 40, § 138</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>spotted like a
				panther</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mensae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					13, 15, 30, § 96</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>cunning</i>, <i>crafty</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pantherinum genus (hominum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ep. 1, 1, 16</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
